{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently underestimates the speed of recovery following sharp price drops (e.g., the drop to ~52-53 EUR), predicting a slow, linear drift instead of the actual rapid V-shaped rebound to 57-60 EUR within 5-7 days.",
    "Adjust for sentiment-ignored volatility: Positive sentiment spikes (value 1.00) in the history are not reflected in the forecast magnitude; the model fails to anticipate the subsequent 10-15 EUR price surge that follows these signals.",
    "Reduce long-horizon overconfidence: The model's 30-day forecast exhibits an artificial, monotonic upward trend that ignores the high-frequency oscillation and eventual peak/trough cycles seen in the true data, leading to significant underestimation in the mid-term (days 10-20) and overestimation in the late-term (days 25-30) relative to the actual peak.",
    "Incorporate momentum after lows: When history shows a steep decline followed by a single day of recovery, the model's immediate next-day forecast should be adjusted upward by at least 2-3 EUR to match the observed momentum, rather than assuming a flat or slightly declining baseline."
  ]
}
